  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Oct 16, 2026 at 03:34 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: Nearly one in four <a href=\"/tag/spine+investigations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">spine investigations</a> conducted between September 2025 and September 2026 involved individuals below the age of 40, data from <a href=\"/tag/mahajan+imaging\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mahajan Imaging</a> &amp; Labs found.Monthly spine investigations also increased by approximately 24% in September 2026 compared with September 2025, rising from 2,156 to 2,677.Mahajan Imaging said the findings highlight that back pain as a concern isn’t limited to older adults.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>A total of 29,532 spine investigations were recorded during the 13-month period.Individuals aged 60 and above accounted for the largest share, with 11,558 investigations, or approximately 39% of the total.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>People aged between 40 and 60 accounted for another 11,049 investigations, representing around 37%, while 6,925 investigations, or nearly 23.5%, involved individuals below 40.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Women accounted for 16,855 investigations, approximately 57% of the total, compared with 12,677 among men.However, the diagnostic firm noted that these figures reflect investigation volumes rather than confirmed diagnoses and should not be interpreted as a measure of disease prevalence.Dr. Harsh Mahajan, Founder &amp; Chairperson, Mahajan Imaging &amp; Labs, and Mentor, FICCI Health,said, “Back pain should not be dismissed simply because a person is young, nor should it automatically be considered an inevitable part of ageing. Prolonged sitting, inadequate movement and poor physical conditioning can contribute to discomfort, but symptoms alone cannot establish the underlying cause. Pain that persists, recurs frequently or begins to interfere with everyday activities warrants medical assessment. \"                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 16, 2026 at 03:34 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 16, 2026 at 03:34 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n   